   C(2, "A thing hammered from scraps", "The forging is the poem's great passage: from swan-feather tips, the milk of barren kine, a grain of barley — scraps of the world made into something magic by skill.", ["mill"], "obj.sam.forge"),
   C(3, "The mill that grinds fortune", "The Sampo is finished: a threefold mill that grinds out flour for food, salt for trade, and money for wealth — prosperity itself, produced on demand.", ["mill"], "obj.sam.mill"),
